From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shm_unlink: report EACCES where unlink fails with EPERM

In a sticky directory such as /dev/shm, unlink of another user's file
fails with EPERM.  POSIX specifies EACCES for shm_unlink when
permission is denied, and glibc translates the error the same way.
Other errors are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/src/mman/shm_open.c b/src/mman/shm_open.c
--- a/src/mman/shm_open.c
+++ b/src/mman/shm_open.c
@@ -39,5 +39,9 @@ int shm_unlink(const char *name)
 {
 	char buf[NAME_MAX+10];
 	if (!(name = __shm_mapname(name, buf))) return -1;
-	return unlink(name);
+	int r = unlink(name);
+	/* unlink fails with EPERM in a sticky directory for another
+	 * user's file; shm_unlink reports denied permission as EACCES. */
+	if (r && errno == EPERM) errno = EACCES;
+	return r;
 }
